{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-client.md | sed -n '240,280p'\"","aggregated_output":"   240\t    participant Switcher as version-switcher.ts\n   241\t    participant Router as bootstrap.ts\n   242\t    participant API as review-workspace-api.ts\n   243\t\n   244\t    Note over Switcher,API: AC-3.3 / AC-3.4 / AC-5.3 / AC-5.4\n   245\t    Switcher->>Router: onSelectVersion(versionId)\n   246\t    Router->>API: GET /review/artifacts/:artifactId?versionId=...\n   247\t    alt 200\n   248\t        API-->>Router: artifact target\n   249\t        Router->>Router: patch target + selection\n   250\t    else 404 ARTIFACT_VERSION_NOT_FOUND\n   251\t        API-->>Router: request error\n   252\t        Router->>API: reload workspace bootstrap with same selection\n   253\t        API-->>Router: 200 workspace with bounded unavailable target\n   254\t        Router->>Router: patch workspace state\n   255\t    end\n   256\t```\n   257\t\n   258\tThe fallback reload is the key client decision in this epic. It preserves the\n   259\tworkspace shell, the target list, and the process context even when a selected\n   260\texplicit version disappears later. Without this step, the client would have to\n   261\tflatten a nuanced stale-selection case into a generic request failure.\n   262\t\n   263\t### Version Switcher Behavior\n   264\t\n   265\t`version-switcher.ts` keeps the same interaction model:\n   266\t\n   267\t- click selection\n   268\t- keyboard listbox navigation\n   269\t- explicit selected/current labels\n   270\t\n   271\tWhat changes is the result handling:\n   272\t\n   273\t- successful explicit selection patches the artifact target directly\n   274\t- failed explicit selection triggers bootstrap reload\n   275\t- zero-version artifacts still render without a version switcher because\n   276\t  `versions.length === 0`\n   277\t\n   278\t## Flow 5: Package Member Selection and Degraded Members\n   279\t\n   280\tPackage review is where Epic 5 most clearly benefits from the aligned model.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
